<title>UK: Sumitomo Trust sets convertible buy back price.</title>
<headline>Sumitomo Trust sets convertible buy back price.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sumitomo Trust and Banking Co Ltd will buy back its 1.75 percent convertible bonds due March 31, 2002 at a price of 87.131 percent, dealer manager Lehman Brothers said in a statement on Monday.</p>
<p>The offer expires at midnight New York time on March 10, the statement said.</p>
<p>When the buy back was announced in February, Sumitomo Trust said it was designed to trim its outstanding debt and strengthen its financial base, while trying to avoid a potential increase in the number of its shares.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7748</p>
</text>
